---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Disclaimer from '~/components/Disclaimer.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '~/config/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${siteConfig.name} — ${siteConfig.tagline}`}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] text-[var(--muted)] uppercase">About</p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 text-5xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-6xl"
        style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'SOFT' 30;"
      >
        A quiet place for everyday reflection.
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Mindful is a small collection of short reads on mental wellbeing. Each essay is meant to be
        finished in the span of a slow cup of tea &mdash; a few minutes of breathing room in the
        middle of an ordinary day.
      </p>

      <p>
        We write about the things that quietly shape us: the way we sleep, the way we worry, the
        ways we show up for the people we love. We aim for warmth over cleverness, and calm over
        urgency.
      </p>

      <h2>What Mindful is not</h2>
      <p>
        Mindful is not therapy. It is not medical advice. It is not a replacement for support from a
        qualified professional. If something you read here moves you toward seeking help, we are
        glad. That is the best thing an essay can do.
      </p>

      <h2>If you need support</h2>
      <p>
        If you are in crisis or thinking about harming yourself, please contact your local emergency
        services or a trusted helpline. You deserve support that meets you where you are.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <Disclaimer variant="card" />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
